tice that I was always thinking  about food whether I was doing the right  thing whether I was doing enough whether  what I had eaten had turned me I'm  healthy again and all this guy I mean  that what I'd eaten had turned me  unhealthy yeah I just got to this point  where I was so focused on health that  had I had one meal or one snack or  something that would I wouldn't have  regularly eaten I would just have his  wave of anxiety that that would send me  backwards and I guess you know put the  weight back on I was really really  fearful of waking up one day and then  realizing oh hang on I've put all my  weight back on Megan's anxieties about  her body began to overwhelm her and her  diet evolved into a series of really  strict rules I was caught up in that  idea of clean eating for me I had made  the decision that anything that was  processed during packets was to be  completely avoided and and it's almost  impossible there were so many decisions  to make and making a decision when all  you can hear is right wrong healthy  unhealthy guilty what good food is and  what bad food is it was just terrifying  it was really overwhelming it was almost  like the actual food on the Shelf was  talking to me  telling me all of its pros and all of  its cons and then the next thing I would  need to go and buy was another voice in  my head  there was one time trying to buy a piece  of steak and the idea of trying to buy a  certain size of steak her certain weight  of steak the decision got soever  whelming that I remember just sort of  blanking out dropping my basket and just  staring for what was about 40 minutes  just 40 40 minutes I knew my  relationship with foods gone beyond  anything that I could I could deal with  myself I needed help from there  Megan consulted several doctors but many  of them praised her for losing weight  and told her to keep running and dieting  still obsessing about her ideal body  image physical symptoms began to appear  [Music]  at your worst poin